      },
      "items": [
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "1",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "HEB 3:1"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "1",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "My Christian brothers and sisters, who also have been called by God! Think of Jesus, whom God sent to be the High Priest of the faith we profess. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "HEB.3.1",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "HEB.3.1"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "2",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "HEB 3:2"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "2",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "note",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "style": "x",
            "caller": "#"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "name": "ref",
              "type": "tag",
              "attrs": {
                "loc": "NUM.12.7"
              },
              "items": [
                {
                  "text": "Num 12.7",
                  "type": "text"
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "He was faithful to God, who chose him to do this work, just as Moses was faithful in his work in God's house. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "HEB.3.2",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "HEB.3.2"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "3",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "HEB 3:3"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "3",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "A man who builds a house receives more honour than the house itself. In the same way Jesus is worthy of much greater honour than Moses. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "HEB.3.3",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "HEB.3.3"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "4",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "HEB 3:4"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "4",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Every house, of course, is built by someone — and God is the one who has built all things. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "HEB.3.4",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "HEB.3.4"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "5",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "HEB 3:5"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "5",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Moses was faithful in God's house as a servant, and he spoke of the things that God would say in the future. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "HEB.3.5",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "HEB.3.5"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "6",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "HEB 3:6"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "6",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "But Christ is faithful as the Son in charge of God's house. We are his house if we keep up our courage and our confidence in what we hope for.",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "HEB.3.6",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "HEB.3.6"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
